    "content": "*Relentless Reckless Forever* was the third Children of Bodom album recorded at Sonic Pump Studios in Helsinki — the environment that Anssi Kippo had adapted to across *Blooddrunk* (2008) and subsequent work. By 2010, the Sonic Pump sessions had a fully established blueprint: mic placement, gain structure, EQ curves, and compression settings for Raatikainen's Pearl MCX kit were accumulated institutional knowledge rather than exploratory decisions.\n\n**Pearl MCX in Sonic Pump's Established Acoustic:**\nThe Pearl Masters MCX's attack-forward shell construction suited Sonic Pump's room character — the MCX's improved shell stiffness producing a more immediate attack transient that Kippo could capture cleanly without significant acoustic treatment. The tighter sustain of the MCX construction also simplified the mix environment: less room ring meant a more defined dry sound that sat more naturally in the keyboard and guitar-dense arrangements.\n\n**Double-Kick Treatment at the Pearl Era Peak:**\n*Relentless Reckless Forever*'s double-kick treatment reflected six years of Kippo / Eliminator knowledge: the kick drum EQ focused on the upper attack transient for intelligibility at the highest velocities, with the low-end handled to avoid competing with Janne Wirman's synth bass and keyboard low frequency content. The Powerstroke 3 head's natural character required less processing than the earlier Iron Cobra / Tama sessions.\n\n**Cymbal Balance in the Refined Mix:**\nThe fully understood A Custom / K Custom setup allowed Kippo to treat the cymbal balance with precision: the A Custom's naturally bright character positioned in the high-mid frequency range to cut through the keyboard density without stridence, the K Custom ride's darker presence mixed to serve the melodic, keyboard-driven sections.",
